  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_40" name="Product Costing and Final Price Approval" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-40 and catalog boundaries; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.14 FR-PRICE-01-18; supporting NFR-SEC-03,08, NFR-REL-03,05-06. Website: index.html loads app/pricing-state.js P.breakdown/cost/setPrice, app/owner.js pricing-settings/overhead controls, app/owner-products.js costing panels and app/earnings-allocation.js analytics estimates. Existing BPMN-37/38/39 and BPMN-26/30 reviewed. SRS authoritative: full rules and visible recovery apply even where prototype is partial. Authorized Owner page access is an entry precondition; no repeated access decision is modeled. Protected requests still enforce permissions automatically. Owner-only process; Staff denied financial data/configuration. Inputs: current variant or applicable costing context, existing final selling price, saved BoM/inventory costs, default/override overhead and markup, versions and Owner request. Utility override wins when present, including zero; otherwise use general default. Packaging is a direct material cost, not added twice. Recipe maintenance is BPMN-39, inventory restock/adjustment/cost-source work is separately owned BPMN-24/25; no such workflow is called automatically merely to read saved cost inputs. BPMN-43 consumes estimates and flags, not a report-generation call during pricing. BPMN-37 consumes saved final catalog prices; BPMN-30 authentication is precondition. All local checks and failure/recovery paths visible, no hidden subprocess, external integration or broadcast. Missing required costing data yields Unavailable, never zero; Owner sees missing-data explanation, may correct through the owning source process and recalculate, retain final price or explicitly select a final price (the SRS does not forbid Owner price selection solely because estimate is unavailable). Negative estimated profit remains visible and is not a price-rejection rule. Estimate recalculations may affect analytics for earlier transactions under FR-PRICE-17; preserve actual original selling amounts/subscription apportionment, payment links, completion dates and owner splits. No payout/payment/inventory movement or automatic final-price overwrite. Proposed atomic save/recovery safeguards are not claims of completed backend implementation.</bpmn:documentation>
