    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Formulas_40">
      <bpmn:text>Cost calculations (FR-PRICE-02–10,16)
Material cost = sum of quantity × unit cost; count packaging once.
Production cost = materials + gas/electricity overhead.
Use product overhead if set; otherwise use the default. Zero is valid.
Suggested price = production cost × (1 + markup/100).
Profit = chosen selling price − production cost.
Margin = profit / chosen selling price × 100, for a positive price.
Exclude delivery, marketing and other nonproduction costs.
Show negative profit. Suggestions never change the final price automatically.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Formulas_40" sourceRef="Calculate_40" targetRef="Formulas_40" associationDirection="None" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Missing_40">
      <bpmn:text>When cost inputs are missing
Check recipe amounts, ingredient/packaging costs and overhead.
Show Unavailable and the missing inputs; never assume zero.
Fix recipes in BPMN-39 and material costs in inventory processes.
Then recalculate, keep the final price, or choose a final price.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Missing_40" sourceRef="Costs_40" targetRef="Missing_40" associationDirection="None" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Preservation_40">
      <bpmn:text>Saved prices and estimates
BPMN-37 uses the saved final selling price.
BPMN-43 uses current cost estimates or Unavailable.
Cost changes may change estimates for earlier purchases.
Keep original purchase amounts, subscription amounts and Owner shares.
No report, payment or payout is created here.
Authorized Owner access is required before entry (BPMN-30).
Protected requests still enforce permissions automatically.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Preservation_40" sourceRef="Expose_40" targetRef="Preservation_40" associationDirection="None" />
  </bpmn:process>
